d C will start cleaning a window at the same time again, we need the least common multiple (LCM) of their cleaning intervals: 8, 12, and 14 minutes.  \nPrime factorizations: 8 = 2³, 12 = 2²×3, 14 = 2×7. The LCM is the highest power of each prime: 2³ × 3 × 7 = 8 × 3 × 7 = 168 minutes.  \n168 minutes = 2 hours 48 minutes, so adding to 14:15 gives 14:15 + 2:48 = 17:03.\n\n\\boxed{17:03}",
