    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the speed of the car starting from A be $ x $ km/h and the speed of the car starting from B be $ y $ km/h.  \nWhen they travel in the same direction, the relative speed is $ |x - y| $, and they meet in 7 hours. Since they start 70 km apart, we have:  \n$ 7|x - y| = 70 $ → $ |x - y| = 10 $.  \nWhen they travel towards each other, the relative speed is $ x + y $, and they meet in 1 hour:  \n$ x + y = 70 $.  \n\nAssuming $ x > y $, then $ x - y = 10 $. Solving the system:  \n$ x + y = 70 $  \n$ x - y = 10 $  \nAdding: $ 2x = 80 $ → $ x = 40 $, then $ y = 30 $.  \n\nThus, the speeds are 40 km/h and 30 km/h.  \n\\boxed{{40, 30}}",
