    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the basic first class full fare be $ F $ and the reservation charge be $ R $.  \nA full ticket costs $ F + R = 216 $, and one full and one half ticket cost $ (F + R) + \\left(\\frac{F}{2} + R\\right) = 327 $.  \nSubstituting $ F + R = 216 $ into the second equation:  \n$ 216 + \\left(\\frac{F}{2} + R\\right) = 327 $ → $ \\frac{F}{2} + R = 111 $.  \nNow subtract this from the first equation:  \n$ (F + R) - \\left(\\frac{F}{2} + R\\right) = 216 - 111 $ → $ \\frac{F}{2} = 105 $ → $ F = 210 $.  \nThen $ R = 216 - 210 = 6 $.\n\nThe basic first class full fare is $ \\boxed{210} $ and the reservation charge is $ \\boxed{6} $.",
