    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Central place theory is most obviously expressed in\n\nOptions: \nA. a pulpit facing a congregation in most synagogues\nB. a city market's location at a transportation node\nC. a ring freeway that encircles a metropolitan area\nD. a school playground located adjacent to the structure\nE. a police station's location closest to the sites of crime\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Central place theory, developed by Walter Christaller, explains the size, number, and distribution of human settlements, emphasizing that central places (like towns or cities) are spatially arranged to provide goods and services to surrounding areas. The theory predicts that such places will be located at central points within a region to maximize accessibility and efficient service distribution. A city market's location at a transportation node aligns with this principle, as it serves a surrounding hinterland and benefits from connectivity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
