    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The bid-rent theory explains how land prices and land use vary with distance from the central business district (CBD) in urban areas. According to this theory, businesses and individuals compete for land based on their ability to pay, with the highest bids typically coming from commercial users in the CBD, leading to the highest land values there. As distance from the CBD increases, land values decrease because accessibility to the city center diminishes, making it less attractive for high-rent commercial activities.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}",
