    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To simplify the expression $\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$, first rewrite $\\sec x$ as $\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$ to get $\\frac{1}{\\sin x \\cos x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$. By finding a common denominator of $\\sin x \\cos x$, the expression becomes $\\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x}$. Using the identity $1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x$, this simplifies to $\\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x$.\n\n\\boxed{\\cot x}",
