    "global index": "MATH_360",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The following line is parameterized, so that its direction vector is of the form $\\begin{{pmatrix}} -7 \\\\ b \\end{{pmatrix}}.$  Find $b.$\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.4 cm);\n\npair A, B, L, R;\nint i, n;\n\nfor (i = -8; i <= 8; ++i) {{\n  draw((i,-8)--(i,8),gray(0.7));\n  draw((-8,i)--(8,i),gray(0.7));\n}}\n\ndraw((-8,0)--(8,0),Arrows(6));\ndraw((0,-8)--(0,8),Arrows(6));\n\nA = (-5,4);\nB = (-1,3);\nL = extension(A, B, (-8,0), (-8,1));\nR = extension(A, B, (8,0), (8,1));\n\ndraw(L--R, red);\n\nlabel(\"$x$\", (8,0), E);\nlabel(\"$y$\", (0,8), N);\n[/asy]\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The line through the points \\(A(-5,4)\\) and \\(B(-1,3)\\) has direction vector  \n\n\\[\n\\vec{AB}=(-1-(-5),\\,3-4)=(4,-1).\n\\]\n\nIf the line is parametrized with direction vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix}-7\\\\ b\\end{pmatrix}\\), this vector must be a scalar multiple of \\((4,-1)\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix}-7\\\\ b\\end{pmatrix}=k\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\ -1\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nFrom the first component, \\(-7=4k\\) giving \\(k=-\\frac{7}{4}\\).  \nThen \\(b = -1\\cdot k = -1\\left(-\\frac{7}{4}\\right)=\\frac{7}{4}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{4}}\n\\]",
