    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A standard deck has 52 cards: 12 face cards (Jack, Queen, King of each suit) and 4 aces.  \nThe probability of drawing a face card first is $ \\frac{12}{52} $. Without replacement, 51 cards remain, and the probability of then drawing an ace is $ \\frac{4}{51} $.  \nSo, the combined probability is $ \\frac{12}{52} \\times \\frac{4}{51} = \\frac{48}{2652} = \\frac{4}{221} $.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
