      "generated_answer": "To find the probability that an observation is between 50 and 55, convert the values to standard $Z$-scores using $Z = (X - \\mu) / \\sigma$, resulting in $Z = (50 - 50) / 10 = 0$ and $Z = (55 - 50) / 10 = 0.5$. Using a standard normal distribution table, the cumulative probability for $Z = 0.5$ is approximately $0.6915$, and for $Z = 0$ is $0.5$. The difference, $0.6915 - 0.5000 = 0.1915$, aligns with option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
