  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3049",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miniature poodles are thought to have a mean height of 12 inches and a standard deviation of 1.8 inches. If height is measured to the nearest inch, find the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. 45 percent\nB. 2.5 percent\nC. 5 percent\nD. 30 percent\nE. 20 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 15 percent\nH. 35 percent\nI. 40 percent\nJ. 25 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we must account for the fact that the height is measured to the nearest inch, which requires a continuity correction.\n\n1.  **Identify the parameters:** The mean height ($\\mu$) is 12 inches, and the standard deviation ($\\sigma$) is 1.8 inches.\n2.  **Determine the cutoff:** Since the height is measured to the nearest inch, a measurement of 14 inches corresponds to a true height in the range $[13.5, 14.5)$. To have a height \"exceeding 14 inches,\" the measurement must be at least 15 inches, which corresponds to a true height of at least 14.5 inches ($x \\ge 14.5$).\n3.  **Calculate the Z-score:**\n    $$Z = \\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma} = \\frac{14.5 - 12}{1.8} = \\frac{2.5}{1.8} \\approx 1.39$$\n4.  **Find the probability:** Using the standard normal distribution, the probability $P(Z > 1.39)$ is approximately $1 - 0.9177 = 0.0823$, or roughly 8.2%.\n5.  **Select the best option:** Among the given choices, 10% (Option F) is the closest value to our calculated result of 8.2%.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 201,
        "output_tokens": 6538,
        "total_tokens": 6739
      },
      "provider": "vertex",
      "error": null
