    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}.\n\nEvolutionary biology posits that natural selection acts as a \"tinker\" rather than an engineer, modifying existing anatomical structures inherited from ancestors rather than designing new systems from scratch. Because these forelimbs are constrained by their evolutionary history and the homology of the ancestral tetrapod limb, they cannot be optimized for every specific environment in the way a bespoke design might be.",
