      "generated_answer": "Since the mother is type O (genotype *ii*) and the child is type O (*ii*), the child must have inherited an *i* allele from the father. A person with type B blood can have the genotype $I^B i$, meaning they are capable of passing on the *i* allele. Therefore, while he cannot be excluded as the father, the blood type result does not definitively confirm paternity.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
