    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4278",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the two most important uses of ammonia is as a reagent in the first step of theOsfwaldprocess, a synthetic route for the production of nitric acid. This first step proceeds according to the equation 4NH_3(g) + 50_2(g) \\rightleftarrows 4N0(g) + 6H_20(g) . What is the expression for the equilibrium constant of this reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. K = {{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}} / {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 }}\nB. K = {{[O_2]^5}} / {{ [NO]^4 [NH_3]^4 [H_2O]^6}}\nC. K = {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 }} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}}\nD. K = {{[NO]^6 [H_2O]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^5 [O_2]^4}}\nE. K = {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 [NH_3]^4}} / {{[O_2]^5}}\nF. K = {{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5 [H_2O]^6}} / {{[NO]^4}}\nG. K = {{[NO]^4 [NH_3]^4}} / {{ [H_2O]^6 [O_2]^5}}\nH. K = {{[NH_3]^5 [O_2]^4}} / {{ [NO]^6 [H_2O]^4}}\nI. K = {{[NO]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}}\nJ. K = {{[NO]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [H_2O]^6}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The equilibrium constant expression for a chemical reaction $aA + bB \\rightleftarrows cC + dD$ is given by the product of the concentrations of the products raised to their stoichiometric coefficients divided by the product of the concentrations of the reactants raised to their stoichiometric coefficients, which is $K = \\frac{[C]^c [D]^d}{[A]^a [B]^b}$. Applying this to the given reaction $4NH_3(g) + 5O_2(g) \\rightleftarrows 4NO(g) + 6H_2O(g)$, we obtain $K = \\frac{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6}{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}$. This matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 489,
        "output_tokens": 457,
