      "generated_answer": "According to the Gibbs phase rule, $F = C - P + 2$, where $F$ is the degrees of freedom, $C$ is the number of components, and $P$ is the number of phases. For a three-component mixture ($C=3$), the maximum number of phases occurs when the degrees of freedom $F$ is zero ($P = 3 - 0 + 2 = 5$). Thus, the maximum number of phases at equilibrium is 5.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
