    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6892",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $f(x)=ax^6-bx^4+x-1$ and $f(2)=5$, then what is the value of $f(-2)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 1\nC. 2\nD. 0\nE. -5\nF. -2\nG. 5\nH. -3\nI. -1\nJ. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2)&=a(2)^6-b(2)^4+2-1=64a-16b+1=5\\\\\n\\Rightarrow&\\;64a-16b=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nNow\n\\[\nf(-2)=a(-2)^6-b(-2)^4-2-1=64a-16b-3.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(64a-16b=4\\) gives \\(f(-2)=4-3=1\\).\n\nThe correct choice is **B**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{B}\n\\]",
