    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given linear system can be written as  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n1 & -\\cos\\gamma & -\\cos\\beta\\\\[2pt]\n-\\cos\\gamma & 1 & -\\cos\\alpha\\\\[2pt]\n-\\cos\\beta & -\\cos\\alpha & 1\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\\begin{pmatrix}a\\\\ b\\\\ c\\end{pmatrix}=0 .\n\\]\n\nSince \\((a,b,c)\\neq(0,0,0)\\), the determinant of the matrix must vanish. Computing the determinant gives  \n\n\\[\n1-(\\cos^2\\alpha+\\cos^2\\beta+\\cos^2\\gamma)-2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma=0,\n\\]\n\nso  \n\n\\[\n\\cos^2\\alpha+\\cos^2\\beta+\\cos^2\\gamma+2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma=1.\n\\]\n\nThus the required value is \\(1.0\\), corresponding to option **D**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}\n\\]",
