    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The reaction free energy is \\(\\Delta G^\\circ =-nF E^\\circ =-(1)(96485\\;\\text{C mol}^{-1})(0.222\\;\\text{V})\\approx-21.4\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}\\).\n\nFor the half‑reaction \\(\\mathrm{AgCl(s)}+e^- \\to \\mathrm{Ag(s)}+\\mathrm{Cl^-}\\),\n\n\\[\n\\Delta G^\\circ = \\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{Ag})+\\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{Cl^-})-\\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{AgCl})\n\\]\n\nwith \\(\\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{Ag})=0\\). Hence  \n\n\\[\n\\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{Cl^-}) = \\Delta G^\\circ + \\mu^\\circ(\\mathrm{AgCl})\n= -21.4\\;\\text{kJ mol}^{-1} + (-109.71\\;\\text{kJ mol}^{-1})\n\\approx -131.1\\;\\text{kJ mol}^{-1}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{C}\n\\]",
