    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8924",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jupiter and the other jovian planets are sometimes called \"gas giants.\" In what sense is this term misleading?\n\nOptions: \nA. They actually contain a significant fraction of non-gaseous matter.\nB. The materials they are made of are not normally gaseous in everyday experience.\nC. They are not giant in size compared to other celestial bodies.\nD. The term 'gas' suggests they are entirely gaseous, but they have solid cores.\nE. Actually it's a great description because these worlds are big and gaseous throughout.\nF. The term 'giant' implies they are the largest planets, which is not always accurate.\nG. Their atmospheres contain more liquids than gases.\nH. They are not made of gas, but rather of heavier elements.\nI. The materials that make up these planets are primarily in the form of a plasma not a gas.\nJ. The term is misleading as it implies they are similar in composition to our planet's gas layer, which is not the case.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
