    "global index": "MathQA_1962",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: let f ( x ) = x ^ 2 + bx + c . if f ( 3 ) = 0 and f ( - 3 ) = 0 , then b + c =\n\nOptions: \nA. 18\nB. 15\nC. - 15\nD. - 21\nE. - 9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given that $ f(x) = x^2 + bx + c $, and $ f(3) = 0 $, $ f(-3) = 0 $.  \nThis means that both $ x = 3 $ and $ x = -3 $ are roots of the quadratic.  \nSo, the quadratic can be written as $ f(x) = (x - 3)(x + 3) = x^2 - 9 $.  \n\nComparing with $ f(x) = x^2 + bx + c $, we get $ b = 0 $ and $ c = -9 $.  \nThus, $ b + c = 0 + (-9) = -9 $.  \n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
