    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: how many internal diagonals does a pentagon ( five sided polygon ) have ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 8\nC. 9\nD. 10\nE. 12\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of internal diagonals in a polygon, use the formula:  \n\\[\n\\frac{n(n - 3)}{2}\n\\]  \nwhere $ n $ is the number of sides. For a pentagon, $ n = 5 $, so:  \n\\[\n\\frac{5(5 - 3)}{2} = \\frac{5 \\times 2}{2} = 5\n\\]  \nThus, the pentagon has 5 internal diagonals.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
