    "global index": "MathQA_2920",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a father said his son , ` ` i was as old as you are at present at the time of your birth . ` ` if the father age is 40 now , the son age 5 years back was\n\nOptions: \nA. 14\nB. 17\nC. 15\nD. 19\nE. 99\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the son's current age be $ x $.  \nAccording to the statement, the father was as old as the son is now at the time of the son's birth. That means:  \nFather's age at son's birth = Son's current age → $ 40 - x = x $ → $ 40 = 2x $ → $ x = 20 $.  \nSo, the son is currently 20 years old. Therefore, 5 years ago, the son was $ 20 - 5 = 15 $ years old.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
