    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When two dice are thrown simultaneously, there are a total of $6 \\times 6 = 36$ possible outcomes.  \nWe need the probability that the sum is greater than 7, i.e., sums of 8, 9, 10, 11, or 12.  \nThe number of favorable outcomes for each sum is:  \n- Sum of 8: (2,6), (3,5), (4,4), (5,3), (6,2) → 5 ways  \n- Sum of 9: (3,6), (4,5), (5,4), (6,3) → 4 ways  \n- Sum of 10: (4,6), (5,5), (6,4) → 3 ways  \n- Sum of 11: (5,6), (6,5) → 2 ways  \n- Sum of 12: (6,6) → 1 way  \nTotal favorable = $5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 15$  \nSo, probability = $ \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12} $\n\n\\boxed{C}",
