    "global index": "MathQA_862",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 10 stickers numbered 1 to 10 are placed in a bowl , mixed up thoroughly and then one sticker is drawn randomly . if it is known that the number on the drawn sticker is more than 3 , what is the probability that it is an even number ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3 / 7\nB. 4 / 7\nC. 5 / 7\nD. 7 / 11\nE. 9 / 11\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given that the sticker drawn has a number greater than 3, so the possible outcomes are the numbers: 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10. This gives a total of 7 possible outcomes. Among these, the even numbers are 4, 6, 8, and 10 — which are 4 in total. Therefore, the probability that the number is even given that it is greater than 3 is 4/7.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
