    "global index": "MathQA_2066",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the total surface area of a solid hemisphere of diameter 14 cm , is :\n\nOptions: \nA. ['a ) 462 cm ²'\nB. 'b ) 530 cm ²'\nC. 'c ) 1345 cm ²'\nD. 'd ) 1788 cm ²'\nE. 'e ) none']\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the total surface area of a solid hemisphere, we use the formula:  \nTotal Surface Area = 3πr², which includes the curved surface area (2πr²) and the flat circular base (πr²).  \nGiven the diameter is 14 cm, the radius r = 7 cm.  \nSo, Total Surface Area = 3 × (22/7) × 7² = 3 × (22/7) × 49 = 3 × 22 × 7 = 462 cm².\n\nThus, the correct answer is option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 162,
        "output_tokens": 134,
        "total_tokens": 296
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
