    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "cost": 2.4902e-05
  },
  {
    "global index": "MathQA_1246",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: for what value of â € œ k â €  will the equation ( 2 kx 2 + 5 kx + 1 ) = 0 have equal roots ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 / 7\nB. 9 / 4\nC. 8 / 25\nD. 7 / 1\nE. 7 / 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the quadratic equation:  \n$ 2kx^2 + 5kx + 1 = 0 $  \nFor a quadratic equation $ ax^2 + bx + c = 0 $ to have equal roots, the discriminant must be zero: $ b^2 - 4ac = 0 $.  \n\nHere, $ a = 2k $, $ b = 5k $, $ c = 1 $.  \nSo, discriminant $ D = (5k)^2 - 4(2k)(1) = 25k^2 - 8k $.  \nSet $ D = 0 $:  \n$ 25k^2 - 8k = 0 $  \n$ k(25k - 8) = 0 $  \nSo, $ k = 0 $ or $ k = \\frac{8}{25} $.  \n\nBut $ k = 0 $ would make the equation $ 1 = 0 $, which is not quadratic and has no solution. So, the valid value is $ k = \\frac{8}{25} $.  \n\nThis matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 163,
        "output_tokens": 248,
        "total_tokens": 411
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
