    "global index": "MathQA_1091",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: from a group of 4 boys and 4 girls , 2 children are to be randomly selected . what is the probability that 1 boy and 1 girl will be selected ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 2\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 5\nD. 4 / 7\nE. 5 / 9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are selecting 2 children from a group of 8 (4 boys and 4 girls). The total number of ways to choose 2 children is $\\binom{8}{2} = 28$. The number of favorable outcomes (1 boy and 1 girl) is $\\binom{4}{1} \\times \\binom{4}{1} = 4 \\times 4 = 16$. So, the probability is $\\frac{16}{28} = \\frac{4}{7}$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
