      "generated_answer": "We are given two quadratic equations that $ x $ must satisfy:\n\n1. $ x^2 + 2x - 24 = 0 $\n2. $ x^2 - 5x + 4 = 0 $\n\nWe solve each equation separately and find the common solution.\n\nFirst, factor $ x^2 + 2x - 24 = 0 $:\n$$\n(x + 6)(x - 4) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = -6 \\text{ or } x = 4\n$$\n\nNow, factor $ x^2 - 5x + 4 = 0 $:\n$$\n(x - 4)(x - 1) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 4 \\text{ or } x = 1\n$$\n\nThe only common solution is $ x = 4 $.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
