    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given that the probability of heads on any flip is $ \\frac{1}{2} $, and each flip is independent. We want the probability of a specific sequence: heads on the first 3 flips and tails on the last 2 flips, i.e., $ HHH TT $.\n\nSince each flip is independent, we multiply the probabilities:  \n$ \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{32} $.\n\nThis is the probability of one specific outcome out of $ 2^5 = 32 $ possible sequences.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
