    "global index": "MathQA_857",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if 2 ^ 2 n + 2 ^ 2 n + 2 ^ 2 n + 2 ^ 2 n = 4 ^ 20 , then n =\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 6\nC. 19\nD. 23\nE. 24\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the equation:\n\n$$\n2^{2n} + 2^{2n} + 2^{2n} + 2^{2n} = 4^{20}\n$$\n\nThere are four identical terms on the left, so:\n\n$$\n4 \\cdot 2^{2n} = 4^{20}\n$$\n\nNote that $4 = 2^2$, so rewrite everything in base 2:\n\n$$\n4 \\cdot 2^{2n} = (2^2)^{20} = 2^{40}\n$$\n\nAlso, $4 = 2^2$, so:\n\n$$\n2^2 \\cdot 2^{2n} = 2^{40} \\Rightarrow 2^{2 + 2n} = 2^{40}\n$$\n\nNow equate exponents:\n\n$$\n2 + 2n = 40 \\Rightarrow 2n = 38 \\Rightarrow n = 19\n$$\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
