    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n = 1 ! + 2 ! + 3 ! . . . . . + 10 ! . what is the last digit of n ^ n ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nD. 6\nE. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the last digit of $n$, we sum the factorials modulo 10: $n \\equiv 1! + 2! + 3! + 4! + 0 + \\dots + 0 \\equiv 1 + 2 + 6 + 24 \\equiv 33 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{10}$. To find the last digit of $n^n$, we determine the exponent modulo 4 (the cycle length of powers of 3 is 4): $n \\equiv 1! + 2! + 3! + 0 + \\dots \\equiv 1 + 2 + 6 \\equiv 9 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$. Therefore, the last digit of $n^n$ is the same as $3^1$, which is 3.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
