    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: on a sum of money , the simple interest for 2 years is rs . 324 , while the compound interest is rs . 340 , the rate of interest being the same in both the cases . the rate of interest is\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 %\nB. 14.25 %\nC. 9.87 %\nD. 10.5 %\nE. 11.5 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The difference between compound interest and simple interest for two years is $Rs. 340 - Rs. 324 = Rs. 16$. Using the relationship formula $\\text{Difference} = SI \\times \\frac{R}{200}$, we substitute the values: $16 = 324 \\times \\frac{R}{200}$. Solving for $R$ yields $R = \\frac{3200}{324} \\approx 9.876\\%$, which matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
