    "global index": "MathQA_2322",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a circle in the coordinate plane passes through points ( - 3 , - 2 ) and ( 1 , - 4 ) . what is the smallest possible area of that circle ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13 π\nB. 26 π\nC. 262 √ π\nD. 5 π\nE. 64 π\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The smallest circle occurs when the center is at the midpoint of the segment joining the two points, giving radius equal to half the distance between them.  \nDistance between \\((-3,-2)\\) and \\((1,-4)\\) is \\(\\sqrt{4^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}\\); thus the minimal radius is \\(\\sqrt{5}\\).  \nArea \\(= \\pi r^{2}= \\pi(5)=5\\pi\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 210,
