  {
    "global index": "MathQA_518",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if f ( f ( n ) ) + f ( n ) = 2 n + 3 and f ( 0 ) = 1 , what is the value of f ( 2012 ) ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 222\nB. 2787\nC. 2013\nD. 2778\nE. 10222\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the functional equation:  \n$$ f(f(n)) + f(n) = 2n + 3 $$  \nand the initial condition:  \n$$ f(0) = 1 $$\n\nLet us assume $ f(n) = an + b $. Try to plug into the equation:  \nThen $ f(f(n)) = a(an + b) + b = a^2n + ab + b $.  \nSo the left-hand side becomes:  \n$$ f(f(n)) + f(n) = a^2n + ab + b + an + b = (a^2 + a)n + (ab + 2b) $$  \nSet equal to $ 2n + 3 $, so:  \n$$ a^2 + a = 2 \\Rightarrow a^2 + a - 2 = 0 \\Rightarrow (a+2)(a-1) = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 1 \\text{ or } a = -2 $$  \nTry $ a = 1 $: then $ ab + 2b = b + 2b = 3b = 3 \\Rightarrow b = 1 $  \nSo $ f(n) = n + 1 $. Check:  \n$ f(f(n)) = f(n+1) = n + 2 $, so $ f(f(n)) + f(n) = n+2 + n+1 = 2n + 3 $. ✔️  \nAlso $ f(0) = 1 $. ✔️  \nSo $ f(n) = n + 1 $ satisfies all conditions.  \nThus, $ f(2012) = 2012 + 1 = 2013 $\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 168,
        "output_tokens": 361,
        "total_tokens": 529
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "cost": 4.8028e-05
  },
