      "generated_answer": "The original cube has surface area \\(6\\cdot5^{2}=150\\text{ cm}^2\\). After cutting into \\(5^3=125\\) unit cubes, total surface area is \\(125\\cdot6=750\\text{ cm}^2\\). The increase is \\(750-150=600\\text{ cm}^2\\), which is \\(\\frac{600}{150}\\times100\\%=400\\%\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}\n\\]",
