    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This statement can be derived from Lagrange's identity when the time derivative of the scalar G function is equal to zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The statement is the **Virial Theorem**. It is derived from the Lagrange identity $\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{d^2 I}{dt^2} = 2T + \\sum \\mathbf{F}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{r}_i$ by setting the time average of the derivative of the scalar function $G = \\sum \\mathbf{p}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{r}_i$ to zero. This fundamental theorem relates the time-averaged kinetic energy of a stable system to its potential energy.\n\n\\boxed{Virial Theorem}",
