    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This phenomenon refers to the influence of **phase fluctuations** (or superconducting phase fluctuations), which prevent the formation of a robust, long-range ordered superconducting state in under-doped cuprates. These fluctuations break the phase coherence required to sustain the characteristic anti-nodal coherence peaks observed in the local density of states. Consequently, as the doping level decreases, the suppression of these peaks signals the transition into a regime dominated by a pseudogap and incoherent pairing.\n\n\\boxed{Phase fluctuations}",
