    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question refers to a condition for a structure $ H $ being a substructure of a series-parallel construct, specifically excluding any structure that contains the wheel graph $ W_4 $ (the wheel on four vertices). Series-parallel graphs are characterized by the absence of certain minors, and it is well known that a graph is series-parallel if and only if it does not contain $ W_4 $ as a minor. Therefore, $ H $ must not contain $ W_4 $ as a substructure or minor to qualify as a substructure of a series-parallel construct.\n\nThus, the correct and most common answer is:\n\n\\boxed{W_4}",
