    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of voice signals that can be multiplexed, we first determine the sampling frequency $f_s$ and the bits per sample $n$. Using the standard sampling rate for voice ($f_s = 8 \\text{ kHz}$), the frame duration is $T_s = 1/8000 = 125 \\mu s$. With $L = 16$ quantization levels, the bits per sample is $n = \\log_2(16) = 4$ bits, and given a bit duration of $T_b = 1 \\mu s$, each signal requires $4 \\mu s$ per frame. The number of signals $N$ is calculated as $N \\leq T_s / (n \\times T_b) = 125 / 4 = 31.25$, which approximates to 30 signals.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
