  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10193",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A card is drawn at random from a deck of cards. Find the probability that at least one of the following three events will occur: Event A : a heart is drawn. Event B: a card which is not a face card is drawn. Event C: the number of spots (if any) on the drawn card is divisible by 3.\n\nOptions: \nA. 40/52\nB. 31/52\nC. 33/52\nD. 44/52\nE. 45/52\nF. 43/52\nG. 30/52\nH. 38/52\nI. 41/52\nJ. 35/52\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are to find the probability that **at least one** of the three events A, B, or C occurs when a card is drawn at random from a standard 52-card deck.\n\nInstead of computing the union directly, it's easier to use the complement:  \nP(A ∪ B ∪ C) = 1 - P(none of the events occur) = 1 - P(not A and not B and not C)\n\n- Not A: card is **not a heart** → 39 cards (clubs, diamonds, spades)\n- Not B: card **is a face card** (Jack, Queen, King) → 3 face cards per suit × 4 suits = 12 face cards\n- Not C: card’s number is **not divisible by 3**. Numbered cards are 2 through 10. Numbers divisible by 3: 3, 6, 9 → so not divisible: 2, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10 → 7 numbers (excluding A, which has no number, and face cards)\n\nBut we want cards that are **not hearts (not A)**, **are face cards (not B)**, and **number not divisible by 3 (not C)**.\n\nSo we want cards that are:\n- Not hearts → clubs, diamonds, spades (3 suits)\n- Face cards → J, Q, K (3 per suit)\n- But also, for not C: we want cards whose number is **not divisible by 3** → but face cards don’t have numbers, so do they qualify?\n\nWait: Event C is “the number of spots (if any) is divisible by 3”. So for face cards and ace, there is **no number**, so C does not occur → so **not C** occurs for face cards and ace.\n\nBut not B is “is a face card”, so we are restricting to face cards.\n\nSo not A and not B and not C means:\n- Not a heart (so clubs, diamonds, spades)\n- Is a face card (J, Q, K)\n- And not C: number not divisible by 3 — but face cards have no number, so C is false → not C is true.\n\nSo **all non-heart face cards** satisfy not A, not B, and not C.\n\nThere are 3 suits (not hearts), 3 face cards per suit → 3 × 3 = 9 cards.\n\nSo P(none occur) = 9/52\n\nThus, P(at least one occurs) = 1 - 9/52 = 43/52\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 244,
        "output_tokens": 560,
