    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10323",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An FM signal ranging fromf_max= 100.02 MHz to f_min= 99.98 MHz is modulated by a 3kHz sine wave. Find (A) The carrier frequencyf_cof the signal. (B) The carrier swing for the signal. (C) The frequency deviation\\Deltafof the signal. (D) The index of modulation \\beta.\n\nOptions: \nA. f_c=100.01MHz, carrier swing=50 kHz, frequency deviation=25 kHz, modulation index=8.333\nB. f_c=100MHz, carrier swing=44 kHz, frequency deviation=22 kHz, modulation index=7.333\nC. f_c=100MHz, carrier swing=70 kHz, frequency deviation=35 kHz, modulation index=11.667\nD. f_c=100MHz, carrier swing=20 kHz, frequency deviation=10 kHz, modulation index=3.333\nE. f_c=100.02MHz, carrier swing=80 kHz, frequency deviation=40 kHz, modulation index=7.5\nF. f_c=100MHz, carrier swing=40 kHz, frequency deviation=20 kHz, modulation index=6.667\nG. f_c=99.98MHz, carrier swing=60 kHz, frequency deviation=30 kHz, modulation index=5\nH. f_c=100MHz, carrier swing=100 kHz, frequency deviation=50 kHz, modulation index=8\nI. f_c=99.99MHz, carrier swing=30 kHz, frequency deviation=15 kHz, modulation index=5\nJ. f_c=99.99MHz, carrier swing=80 kHz, frequency deviation=40 kHz, modulation index=13.333\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The carrier frequency $f_c$ is the average of $f_{max}$ and $f_{min}$, calculated as $(100.02 + 99.98) / 2 = 100$ MHz. The carrier swing is $f_{max} - f_{min} = 40$ kHz, which leads to a frequency deviation $\\Delta f$ of $40 / 2 = 20$ kHz. The modulation index $\\beta$ is $\\Delta f / f_m = 20 \\text{ kHz} / 3 \\text{ kHz} \\approx 6.667$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
