    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gas a, liters^2 -atm/mole b, liters/mole A 4.0 0.027 B 12.0 0.030 C 6.0 0.032 Which gas has (a) the highest critical temperature, (b) the largest molecular volume, and (c) most ideal general behavior around STP?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gas B has the highest critical temperature, Gas A has the largest molecular volume, Gas C has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nB. Gas B has the highest critical temperature, Gas C has the largest molecular volume, Gas A has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nC. Gas A has the highest critical temperature, Gas B has the largest molecular volume, Gas C has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nD. Gas C has the highest critical temperature, Gas B has the largest molecular volume, Gas A has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nE. Gas A has the highest critical temperature, Gas C has the largest molecular volume, Gas B has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nF. Gas C has the highest critical temperature, Gas A has the largest molecular volume, Gas B has the most ideal general behavior around STP\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
