    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Pain is a subjective experience that lacks an objective biological biomarker or medical instrument for measurement. Because healthcare staff cannot physically \"see\" or measure pain independently, the patient's self-report serves as the gold standard for assessment and treatment. Therefore, the lack of an objective measurement method necessitates reliance on the patient's own description.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
