    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_4869",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The docility hypothesis is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Those who experience low environmental demands become less docile\nB. Those with less capability are less vulnerable to environmental demands\nC. Those with low capabilities are more vulnerable to environmental demands\nD. Those with high capabilities become less vulnerable to environmental demands\nE. Those with high capabilities are more vulnerable to environmental demands\nF. Those who experience high environmental demands become less docile\nG. Those with high capability become less docile in low environmental demands\nH. Those who experience low environmental demands become more docile\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The docility hypothesis, as proposed by M. Powell Lawton, states that as an individual's competence (capability) decreases, their behavior is increasingly governed by the environmental press. Therefore, individuals with lower capabilities are more susceptible to the influence of their surroundings.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
