    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "World Systems Theory defines semi-periphery countries as those that exhibit a mix of core and periphery characteristics, serving as a buffer in the global economy. Unlike periphery nations, which rely primarily on raw material extraction and agriculture, semi-periphery countries have begun to develop manufacturing and industrial sectors, leading to a more diversified economy. Option I is the best choice because it describes the transition toward economic maturity and industrialization that characterizes the semi-periphery.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
