  {
    "global index": "MedMCQA_487",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For statistical test output of p value is interpreted as\n\nOptions: \nA. Rejective Ho, p <0.05\nB. Rejective Ho, p>0.05\nC. Rejective H1, p<0.05\nD. Accepting Ho, p<0.05\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In hypothesis testing, a p-value less than the significance level (typically 0.05) indicates that the observed data are statistically significant, leading to the rejection of the null hypothesis ($H_0$). When $p < 0.05$, there is sufficient evidence to conclude that the null hypothesis is unlikely to be true. Therefore, the standard interpretation is to reject $H_0$ when $p < 0.05$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
