    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The primary cause of radiation-induced dental caries (radiation caries) is xerostomia, or the significant reduction in salivary flow, which eliminates the protective, buffering, and remineralizing properties of saliva. While direct radiation affects the tooth, the rapid onset of decay is clinically attributed to the harsh oral environment created by salivary gland damage. Therefore, the decrease in salivary flow is the initiating and most significant factor.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
