    "global index": "MedMCQA_1513",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of following will happen with a flexible major connector:\n\nOptions: \nA. It will make other components more effective\nB. Will cause PDL destruction of abutment teeth\nC. Cause ill-fitting of RPD\nD. Will cause difficulty in occlusion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A major connector must be rigid to ensure that occlusal forces are effectively distributed across the entire dental arch. If a major connector is flexible, it fails to distribute these stresses, resulting in excessive forces being transferred directly to the abutment teeth. This overloading causes trauma and eventual destruction of the periodontal ligament (PDL) supporting those teeth.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
