    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hormone Replacement therapy is not indicated in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hot flashes\nB. Prevention of CAD\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Vaginal atrophy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT) is FDA-approved for the treatment of moderate to severe vasomotor symptoms (hot flashes), the treatment of vulvar and vaginal atrophy, and the prevention of postmenopausal osteoporosis. However, major clinical trials, such as the Women's Health Initiative (WHI), demonstrated that HRT does not provide cardiovascular protection and may actually increase the risk of cardiovascular events in older women. Therefore, it is no longer indicated for the primary or secondary prevention of Coronary Artery Disease (CAD).\n\n\\boxed{B}",
