    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following drugs is least efficacious in the treatment of temporal lobe epilepsy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Phenobarbitone\nB. Phenytoin sodium\nC. Primidone\nD. Carbamazepine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Carbamazepine, Phenytoin, and Primidone are well-established, first-line, or effective adjuvant medications for the treatment of temporal lobe (focal) epilepsy. Phenobarbitone, while effective, is often considered less favorable and less efficacious for this specific seizure type compared to the others due to its significant sedative and cognitive side effects and the availability of more targeted agents. Therefore, among the provided options, phenobarbitone is generally regarded as having the least favorable efficacy-to-tolerability profile for temporal lobe epilepsy.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
