    "global index": "MedMCQA_1547",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In fracture of atrophic mandible with bone loss, what is the best treatment modality?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bone grafting and load bearing\nB. Bone grafting and load sharing\nC. Semi-rigid fixation\nD. IMF with open reduction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nIn atrophic mandibles with significant bone loss, structural support is compromised, necessitating bone grafting to restore volume and rigid load-bearing fixation (typically a reconstruction plate) to stabilize the fracture during healing. Load-bearing systems are essential because the atrophied bone is insufficient to share the mechanical stress of function. Other options fail to provide the necessary stability for union in a reduced-height mandible.",
