    "global index": "MedMCQA_2065",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the least important prognostic factor in congenital diaphragmatic hernia ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pulmonary Hypertension\nB. Delay in emergent surgery\nC. Size of defect\nD. Gestational age at diagnosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Current literature indicates that once the patient is stabilized, the timing of surgery (specifically, a delay in emergent surgery) does not significantly impact mortality or morbidity compared to stabilization and delayed repair. In contrast, pulmonary hypertension, the size of the defect (which correlates with lung hypoplasia), and the gestational age at diagnosis are critical predictors of survival. Therefore, the timing of the surgery is considered the least important prognostic factor.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
