    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the most reliable method for monitoring fluid resuscitation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Urine output\nB. CVP\nC. Pulse rate\nD. Blood pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Urine output is considered the most reliable clinical indicator of adequate end-organ perfusion during fluid resuscitation. Unlike blood pressure or heart rate, which can be affected by various compensatory mechanisms, urine output directly reflects the status of renal perfusion. Central venous pressure is often unreliable for predicting fluid responsiveness.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
