    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many ways are there to reduce the E-B interval to a diminished fifth?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 3\nC. 4\nD. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The interval E-B is a perfect fifth (7 semitones). To reduce it to a diminished fifth (6 semitones), the net change in pitch must be -1 semitone. This can be achieved by altering the bottom note (E) and/or top note (B) by various accidentals such that the difference in semitone adjustments satisfies the condition. All valid combinations within standard double accidentals yield four possibilities: E-Bb, E#-B, Eb-Bbb, and E##-B#. \n\n\\boxed{C}",
