      "generated_answer": "John Frere's discovery at Hoxne, Suffolk, in 1797 was historically significant because it provided early evidence that humans existed alongside extinct animals. By finding flint tools in the same geological strata as the remains of these creatures, he challenged contemporary beliefs about the age of humanity.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
