    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4643",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The possibility that Homo erectus possessed an aesthetic sense and may have created “art” is suggested by:\n\nOptions: \nA. the discovery of figurines made from clay at the Trinil site.\nB. recovery of a shell at the Trinil site with an intentionally engraved series of lines.\nC. the use of complex tools requiring a high level of cognitive function.\nD. cave paintings and elaborate burials with numerous grave goods at the Trinil site.\nE. all of the above.\nF. all of the above except B and D.\nG. evidence of musical instruments found at the Trinil site.\nH. their ability to control fire, suggesting a deeper understanding of their environment.\nI. the construction of elaborate shelters, indicating a sense of design.\nJ. the size of their brains, with a mean brain size slightly larger than modern humans.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The evidence for this claim specifically refers to a fossil freshwater mussel shell found at the Trinil site in Java, which features a zigzag geometric pattern etched into its surface and is estimated to be around 500,000 years old. This discovery predates similar symbolic behavior previously attributed only to modern humans or Neanderthals. The other options are incorrect as they either refer to later developments, archaeological inaccuracies, or general cognitive traits that do not serve as specific evidence for \"art\" in the context of *Homo erectus*.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
