    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4800",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Egyptian system of hieroglyphics:\n\nOptions: \nA. was a simple form of writing with one symbol representing one word\nB. all of the above\nC. appears to have developed suddenly\nD. did not use pictographs\nE. was borrowed from the Sumerians\nF. was only deciphered in the 20th century\nG. was only used for religious texts\nH. was replaced by the Latin alphabet during the Roman period\nI. was the earliest form of writing in the world\nJ. was only used by the royal family\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Egyptian system of hieroglyphics appears in the archaeological record in a remarkably well-developed state, lacking the clear, lengthy period of evolutionary transition seen in other early writing systems. While other options are demonstrably false—such as the claim that hieroglyphics were the earliest form of writing or that they were deciphered only in the 20th century—the sudden appearance of the script remains a notable subject of historical discussion.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
