    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4516",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is believed to be the reason for the development of a complex society at Caral in South America?\n\nOptions: \nA. the construction of canals for irrigation\nB. the creation of a trade network for llama products\nC. the need to collect large quantities of shellfish\nD. the building of the Piramide Mayor\nE. the need for a centralized defense against invaders\nF. the desire to establish an astronomical observatory\nG. the excavating work to produce the sunken plazas\nH. the development of a hierarchical religious system\nI. the requirement for large-scale stone quarries\nJ. the invention of a complex writing system\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The development of the complex society at Caral is largely attributed to the implementation of extensive irrigation systems, which allowed for the mass cultivation of cotton in the arid Supe Valley. This cotton was essential for creating the large nets required for industrial-scale fishing, enabling a highly productive trade relationship between inland agriculturalists and coastal fishing communities. This agricultural foundation provided the surplus and economic stability necessary for the growth of a sophisticated, complex society.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
