    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4557",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Markings found on the mud-bricks of Huaca del Sol are probably:\n\nOptions: \nA. instructions for the builders written there by the engineers.\nB. random scratches and not a meaningful script or written language.\nC. intended to identify the local group that had produced them.\nD. simple arithmetic performed by carpenters on the building site.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Archaeological research at the Moche site of Huaca del Sol indicates that the thousands of distinct symbols found on adobe bricks functioned as \"maker's marks.\" These marks are widely interpreted by scholars as identifiers for the various community groups (ayllus) that contributed bricks as a form of labor tax to the state. Therefore, the markings served to keep track of the specific groups that produced the building materials.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
