      "generated_answer": "Research at Ceibal has revealed that monumental construction began as early as 1000 BC, which is contemporaneous with or predates similar developments at major Olmec sites like La Venta. This finding challenges the long-standing \"Olmec-mother-culture\" hypothesis, which suggests that the Maya adopted monumental architecture from the Olmecs. Consequently, the timing of these structures points toward an independent, internal development of Maya civilization.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
