    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4708",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pizarro was able to subdue the entire Inca empire largely because:\n\nOptions: \nA. the Incas were suffering from a plague when Pizarro arrived.\nB. the empire had never won the allegiance of the peoples it had conquered.\nC. the Incas were already weakened by a civil war.\nD. the Incas were expecting Pizarro and willingly surrendered to him.\nE. he arrived with a superior force of more than 80,000 soldiers.\nF. Pizarro used advanced technology that the Incas could not comprehend.\nG. his horses and guns frightened the Incas into submission.\nH. Pizarro had the support of other native tribes who were enemies of the Incas.\nI. he was such a brilliant military strategist.\nJ. Pizarro manipulated the Incas into believing he was a god.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "While many factors contributed to the Spanish conquest, the most significant immediate cause was that the Inca Empire was fractured and devastated by a recent civil war between the brothers Atahualpa and Huáscar. This internal conflict left the empire politically divided and militarily depleted when Pizarro arrived.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
