    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4791",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nGunpowder Weaponry: Europe vs. China\nIn Western Europe during the 1200s through the 1400s, early cannons, as heavy and as slow to fire as they were, proved useful enough in the protracted sieges that dominated warfare during this period that governments found it sufficiently worthwhile to pay for them and for the experimentation that eventually produced gunpowder weapons that were both more powerful and easier to move. By contrast, China, especially after the mid-1300s, was threatened mainly by highly mobile steppe nomads, against whom early gunpowder weapons, with their unwieldiness, proved of little utility. It therefore devoted its efforts to the improvement of horse archer units who could effectively combat the country's deadliest foe.\nThe argument in this passage most closely relates to which of the following large-scale questions about global history?\n\nOptions: \nA. Why Silk Road commerce dwindled across the breadth of Eurasia after 1500 C.E.\nB. How societies shared strategically important technologies with each other\nC. How the threat of steppe nomads shaped China's military strategy in the 1300s\nD. Why China and Europe had different military strategies during the Middle Ages\nE. How the medieval climatic optimum affected the process of cultural diffusion\nF. Why European states went on to attain military superiority over non-Western powers in the modern era\nG. How the development of gunpowder weaponry influenced the outcomes of wars in the Middle Ages\nH. How the geopolitical environment influenced the development of military technology in different regions\nI. Why China chose to invest in horse archer units instead of gunpowder weaponry during the medieval period\nJ. How the development of gunpowder weaponry was influenced by the economic status of countries\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage compares how specific regional threats—protracted sieges in Europe versus mobile steppe nomads in China—dictated the divergent paths of military technological development in each region. Therefore, it directly addresses the broader historical inquiry into how geographic and geopolitical contexts shape the evolution of technology.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
