      "generated_answer": "A first-in-first-out (FIFO) queue processes elements in the order they are added, which means the oldest unprocessed node is explored next. Breadth-first search (BFS) explores all nodes at the current depth level before moving to nodes at the next depth level, which requires a FIFO queue to ensure this order. Depth-first search uses a stack (LIFO), and bidirectional search typically uses BFS or DFS from both ends.\n\nThus, the correct answer is breadth-first search.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
